module angle_crossings

// angle_crossings.ri — IDIOM: an angle reading of an ARC-MEASURE ratio is an
// explicit crossing — multiply by `1rad` to ENTER Angle, divide by `1rad` to
// LEAVE it.
//
//     let theta : Angle  = (s / r) * 1rad      // ENTER: ratio -> Angle
//     let ratio          = theta / 1rad        // LEAVE: Angle -> ratio
//     let arc   : Length = r * theta / 1rad    // s = r*theta/eta
//
// WHICH RATIO — read this before reaching for `* 1rad`. The crossing above is
// for an ARC-MEASURE ratio (`s / r`, a length over a length that IS an angle
// in radians). A TRIGONOMETRIC ratio already has a named producer and needs no
// crossing at all: `atan`, `atan2`, `asin`, `acos` and the geometry `angle` /
// `angle_between_surfaces` queries all return Angle directly. `* 1rad` is one
// row of the crossing catalogue in `docs/legibility/design-invariants.md`, not
// the whole of it. The two readings are BOTH legal and give DIFFERENT angles —
// `theta` and `theta_trig` below are built from the same 2.5 ratio and differ,
// which is why picking the wrong one is a silent modelling bug, not a type
// error. Putting the crossing on a producer's result IS caught:
//
//     let bad : Angle = atan(s / r) * 1rad
//         -> error: declared `Scalar[rad]` but its initializer evaluates to
//            `Scalar[rad^2]`
//
// ANTI-PATTERN this replaces:
//     let theta : Angle  = s / r               // don't
//     let arc   : Length = r * theta           // don't
//     let x              = 2.5 * 1 rad         // don't (spaced literal)
//
// Neither of the first two is a style preference — both are hard errors, and
// the third does not parse. Measured with a built `reify check`.
//
// CANONICAL COPY: this block. The verbatim compiler wording lives here, and the
// gate that keeps it verbatim is
// `crates/reify-compiler/tests/harness_doc_chunks/angle_crossings_diagnostics_smoke.rs`,
// which SCRAPES the four transcriptions below out of this comment and asserts
// each one equals what the compiler and parser actually emit for a minimal
// fixture. Reword a diagnostic and that test goes red rather than this block
// rotting silently.
//
// `crates/reify-mcp/src/tools/chunks/units.md` paraphrases the SHAPE of these
// errors rather than re-quoting them, except for the one parse error it quotes
// verbatim — which the same test pins against this block. If a diagnostic is
// reworded, re-measure here first and let the chunk follow; that precedence is
// enforced, not aspirational.
//
//     let   theta : Angle = s / r
//         -> error: let binding 'theta' declared `Scalar[rad]` but its
//            initializer evaluates to `Real`; declared type and initializer
//            type must agree
//     param theta : Angle = s / r
//         -> error: parameter 'theta' declared `Scalar[rad]` but its
//            initializer evaluates to `Real`; declared type and initializer
//            dimension must agree
//     let   arc   : Length = r * theta
//         -> error: let binding 'arc' declared `Scalar[m]` but its initializer
//            evaluates to `Scalar[m·rad]`; declared type and initializer type
//            must agree
//     let   x = 2.5 * 1 rad
//         -> Parse error: syntax error: rad
//
// Drop the annotation on the arc-length case and the error becomes silence
// instead: `let arc = r * theta` evaluates clean to `0.005 m·rad` — a value
// that is not a Length and will not compose with one. The `/ 1rad` is what
// discharges it; the residual itself is recorded in
// `docs/legibility/design-invariants.md` under "Crossing catalogue and
// identities" (the `s = rθ/η` identity and the arc-length discharge note),
// which is the durable owner of this case. Teaching it is the whole remedy —
// no enforcement is possible or chartered.
//
// ALWAYS THE NO-SPACE LITERAL FORM — `1rad`, never `1 rad`.
//
// Verified contracts:
//
//   ENTERING and LEAVING are the same one constant, eta = 1 rad, applied in
//   the two directions. `(s / r)` is dimensionless; `* 1rad` is the named
//   crossing that asserts the quotient is an arc measure. Nothing else in the
//   language will manufacture `rad` for you from a ratio — see
//   `docs/legibility/design-invariants.md`, INV-AD-1 `angle-crossings-explicit`
//   and INV-AD-2 `quotient-pure-derivative-algebra`. The named-crossing
//   catalogue is in that file under "Crossing catalogue and identities"; this
//   exemplar is the hand-rolled `.ri` row of it.
//
//   `omega` is a DIFFERENT crossing class. `2*pi * f * 1rad` carries 2*pi rad/cycle,
//   not eta — see "The 2π rad/cycle distinction (D4)" in the same file. There
//   is no `cycle` unit to write; the typed layer is what forces the
//   distinction, because Frequency and AngularVelocity are different types and
//   one will not silently stand in for the other.
//
//   WHY TORQUE IS N·m/rad and not N·m: same crossing. Work is tau * theta, and
//   theta carries rad, so tau must carry rad^-1 for the product to close on
//   Energy. INV-AD-1 in `docs/legibility/design-invariants.md` is the general
//   form of that argument and its durable owner. This is the WHY only — how to
//   SPELL a torque literal is not taught here.
//
// HONEST ABOUT ENFORCEMENT — this is enforced at an ANNOTATED binding over an
// EXPRESSION, not universally. A bare LITERAL still widens silently:
//     param theta : Angle = 2.5      -> evaluates to `2.5`, dimension erased
//     sin(<dimensionless 2.5>)       -> 0.5984721441039565, accepted
// So the annotations below are load-bearing: each one is the assertion. See
// "Enforcement honesty (D7)" in `docs/legibility/design-invariants.md` for what
// is and is not mandatory today.

structure def AngleCrossings {
    param s : Length    = 5mm
    param r : Length    = 2mm
    param f : Frequency = 50Hz
    param phi : Angle   = 30deg

    // THE IDIOM: `* 1rad` to enter, `/ 1rad` to leave. Each annotation is an
    // assertion — remove the crossing and the binding stops compiling.
    let theta : Angle           = (s / r) * 1rad     // 2.5 rad
    let ratio                   = theta / 1rad       // 2.5
    let arc   : Length          = r * theta / 1rad   // 0.005 m
    let omega : AngularVelocity = 2*pi * f * 1rad    // 314.1592653589793 rad·s^-1

    // NOT a crossing — a named producer. Same 2.5 ratio as `theta`, a
    // different angle: the arc-measure reading and the trigonometric reading
    // are not interchangeable, and no `* 1rad` belongs here.
    let theta_trig : Angle      = atan(s / r)        // 1.1902899496825317 rad

    // FORWARD DIRECTION — the case an author reaching for `s = r*theta`
    // actually has: an angle known independently, not one recovered from a
    // ratio. `arc` above round-trips — `r * (s/r)` is `s` by construction, so
    // it pins the crossing algebra but not the arithmetic. `arc2` does not.
    let arc2  : Length          = r * phi / 1rad     // 0.0010471975511965976 m

    // Bands, not sign guards. A regression that preserved dimensions but moved
    // magnitudes would still satisfy `arc > 0mm`; these fail `reify check`
    // instead, so each identity above is pinned by a predicate and not only by
    // a comment. HONEST SCOPE: `reify check` is the enforcer, and no CI gate
    // runs it over this corpus — `examples_smoke.rs` compiles only, and the
    // two `reify-eval` corpus sweeps assert zero stale-Undef and zero
    // snapshot/cache divergence, never constraint status. What these bands
    // pin is the per-file `reify check` SKILL.md already mandates before
    // shipping a design. A corpus-wide constraint gate is in flight as #6215;
    // if it lands, the no-CI-gate half of this paragraph is stale — re-measure
    // before repeating it.
    constraint r > 0mm
    constraint s > r
    constraint f > 0Hz
    constraint ratio > 2.4              // enter then leave round-trips to s/r
    constraint ratio < 2.6
    constraint arc > 4.9mm              // s = r*theta/eta
    constraint arc < 5.1mm
    constraint arc2 > 1.04mm            // forward: r*phi/eta, phi = pi/6
    constraint arc2 < 1.05mm
    constraint omega > 314.0rad_per_s   // 2*pi*f — the 2*pi rad/cycle class
    constraint omega < 314.3rad_per_s
    constraint theta_trig < theta       // trig reading != arc-measure reading
}
